{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1394707-painting-strange-landscapes-how-weird-is-weird","id":1394707,"title":"Painting Strange Landscapes - How Weird is Weird?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-06T20:25:23-07:00","id":1394707,"title":"Painting Strange Landscapes - How Weird is Weird?","content":"Rereading the chapter fiction for Book of the Deceived brought this question to my mind for a particular chunk of the cosmology, but it bears asking for more accessible locales, too:<br /> <br /> How do you square the notion of supernatural worlds being hostile and alien to human sensibilities with the need to present a coherent-enough setting for gamelines whose monsters interact semiregularly with those places and their inhabitants?<br /> <br /> Starting from the most extreme example: 1e presented much of the &quot;literal gods live here&quot; parts of the cosmology as very\u2026 psychedelic? surreal? And some of that can be laid at the feet of trying to parse the gnostic truths of a horror setting through the lens of an unfamiliar human perspective, given that much of the less in-character material tends to put forward a more cleanly-described vision (for example, I've said elsewhere that for the most part Arcadia functions more like a myth than an acid trip if you're not stuck in the middle of it without the wider context), but trying to bridge these two presentations puts me in the awkward position of not knowing how much I should actually know about the thing I'm making a disconcerting word-picture of.<br /> <br /> In closer-to-ground-level terms, the Shadow is routinely described as alien, and its denizens' priorities are distinctly not human ones, but it's also pretty consistently described as largely reflective of the natural order found on Earth \u2014 magath don't happen with every displaced spirit because eating the closest source of Essence regardless of how appropriate it is is simply <i>not reflective of how most things work</i>, rites tap into an expansive tapestry of oaths and rituals by which the Shadow represents the turning of the seasons et al, the most dangerous bits of spiritual geography are borders between types of territory, etc. Short of getting really good at trawling the internet for esoteric associations to mine for bans and banes and figuring out where to deploy them, I'm not sure how to present the Shadow as simultaneously unfamiliar territory and a place where a werewolf can look at a spirit and think (rightly or wrongly), &quot;Oh, it's a greater tool-spirit. If I leave it to its business it should leave me be while I set up my ambush.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any advice for this sort of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T02:02:27-07:00","id":1394735,"title":"","content":"As you said, this places are alien to HUMAN sensibility.<br /> You can depict the horror and hostility of the shadow for a human, but for a werewolf it s only a dangerous hunting ground, mysterious sometimes but mostly familiar.<br /> The trick for me is to describe the place with sensorial details that for a normal person would be disturbing, but putting emphasis on how the monstrous part of the character is used or even like it.<br /> Anyway it s a complex question, and i m not sure to have understanded all the details you intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T13:54:29-07:00","id":1394847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1394707-painting-strange-landscapes-how-weird-is-weird#post1394707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of getting really good at trawling the internet for esoteric associations to mine for bans and banes and figuring out where to deploy them, I'm not sure how to present the Shadow as simultaneously unfamiliar territory and a place where a werewolf can look at a spirit and think (rightly or wrongly), &quot;Oh, it's a greater tool-spirit. If I leave it to its business it should leave me be while I set up my ambush.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any advice for this sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Play up the predatory. Tool spirit wants. It wants to be used in the ambush. Or to stall or escape an ambush. And of course the preparation for the ambush draws the attention of violence spirits that then gobble that tool up and become slightly more inclined to be tool of violence spirits.<br /> <br /> This goes into the 'Without having to do research' part, but not all spirits are going to be immediately recognizable for what they are, especially given the conceptual aspect to them. A tool spirit could appear as a mad swiss army knife without the red siding, shifting through a variety of metal objects that don't quite seem like their physical reflection. While a hammer may seem like just an object one uses to nail things, it's also known for making horrendous amounts of noise, so offer it a rhythmic smashing.<br /> <br /> You'd also want to keep the background as background, and have the foreground be the more interactive part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T14:53:29-07:00","id":1401197,"title":"","content":"Get a copy of &quot;City Magick&quot; by Christopher Penczak. Do exercise 10. Travel to the Sky City. Do exercise 11. Travel to the Hidden City. Do exercise 27. Meeting the City. Use these personnel experiences to describe to your players what they are seeing/sensing. If you have any drawing skills make your own sketches and add them to those you've printed off the internet.<br /> <br /> Be sure to share as much of your experiences with the exercises here on the forum as you can. Tell us also how you adapted those experiences to use in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}